# A mortal wound taken inside a visit ends the run, and the run cannot be continued.
#
# Wounds had no standing check anywhere. Starvation is caught where vital heat is drawn on a journey
# and age on the return to the map, because those clocks move nowhere else — but a wound is dealt at
# any moment of a visit, by a fight or by the penalty a failed act samples, and nothing looked. A
# protagonist could take a mortal wound from a failed act and go on playing at zero health.
#
# `wound` is the narration counterpart of `fight-wound`. A wound is SAMPLED from a verb's failure
# penalties, one slot in five, so whether a given failed act injures anybody is not something a
# script can ask for — let alone three times over on one body. What wants testing is the consequence.
# cli/outcome/wound_infliction/success.cli covers the sampling itself, at a seed where it lands.
#
# The two assertions at the end are the same pair the other three death scripts make (see
# death_wounds.cli, death_starvation.cli, death_old_age.cli): the screen names the cause, and the
# save is gone before END RUN is pressed rather than when it is.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Hall" --period dawn --save-path .tmp-cli-save/death-narration.json

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

inspect wounds
expect-no-state wounds wound

# Enough to consume the health the frame affords — what a run of bad failures would do.
wound protagonist

# No click, no phase boundary: the check is standing, so the run ends on the next tick.
wait mode Death 45
expect MORTAL WOUNDS
expect END RUN

# Permadeath, as for every other cause.
expect-state savefile save none

click end-run
wait mode MainMenu 20
inspect menu
expect-state menu Continue disabled

quit
